From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_balloon: finer and faster free-page reporting

0004's order-9 (2 MiB) reporting still strands sub-2MiB fragments - the
common state once a guest has run for a while (the "30 MiB used but
130 MiB on host" gap is mostly fragmented free + cache the host never
hears about). And the stock 2s reporting delay keeps freed guest memory
resident on the host for seconds after every free burst.

- Reporting order 9 -> 2 (16 KiB on 4K pages): captures nearly all
  fragmentation without the per-page virtqueue overhead of order-0.
  Still overridable at boot via page_reporting.page_reporting_order=.
- Reporting delay 2s -> 500ms so host RSS converges much closer to
  guest used after free bursts.

Only active when the host negotiates F_REPORTING (honest note:
Firecracker's classic balloon path uses amount_mib inflate + stats and
currently ignores F_REPORTING/F_FREE_PAGE_HINT - the 0002/0003/0006/0007
reclaim paths are what move the needle there; this patch helps hosts
that do enable reporting).

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c | 11 +++++++----
 mm/page_reporting.c             |  7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
index 123456789023..123456789024 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -1095,13 +1095,15 @@
 		vb->pr_dev_info.order = 5;
 #elif PAGE_SHIFT == 12
 		/*
-		 * Aggressive: report 2MB blocks instead of the default
+		 * Aggressive: report 16KB blocks instead of the default
 		 * pageblock-sized ones, so fragmented free memory that can't
-		 * coalesce into a full pageblock is still reported to the
-		 * host. 2MB also matches the host THP size, avoiding splits.
+		 * coalesce is still reported to the host. Order-9 (2MB)
+		 * still stranded sub-2MB fragments - the common case once
+		 * a guest has run for a while. Order-2 captures nearly all
+		 * fragmentation without the per-page overhead of order-0.
 		 * (Overridable at boot via page_reporting.page_reporting_order.)
 		 */
-		vb->pr_dev_info.order = 9;
+		vb->pr_dev_info.order = 2;
 #endif
 
 		err = page_reporting_register(&vb->pr_dev_info);
diff --git a/mm/page_reporting.c b/mm/page_reporting.c
index 123456789025..123456789026 100644
--- a/mm/page_reporting.c
+++ b/mm/page_reporting.c
@@ -47,7 +47,12 @@
  */
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(page_reporting_order);
 
-#define PAGE_REPORTING_DELAY	(2 * HZ)
+/*
+ * MicroVM: report free pages 4x faster. Stock 2s delay keeps freed guest
+ * memory resident on the host for seconds after every free burst;
+ * 500ms converges host RSS much closer to guest used.
+ */
+#define PAGE_REPORTING_DELAY	(HZ / 2)
 static struct page_reporting_dev_info __rcu *pr_dev_info __read_mostly;
 
 enum {

-- 
2.47.0
